WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:04.070
Welcome, and thank you for observing
today.

2
00:00:04.370 --> 00:00:07.243
Here is your role, your screen, notes,

3
00:00:07.243 --> 00:00:11.520
messages, and what to do if something goes
wrong.

4
00:00:12.070 --> 00:00:14.098
You joined like everyone else,

5
00:00:14.098 --> 00:00:19.050
with the room screen's code or the join
link, and chose Observer.

6
00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:24.760
Remember: this exercise tests the plan,
not individuals.

7
00:00:27.310 --> 00:00:29.189
You watch and take notes.

8
00:00:29.189 --> 00:00:34.990
You don't answer injects or guide the
team, even when they are stuck.

9
00:00:35.290 --> 00:00:38.870
What you see becomes the report's
evidence.

10
00:00:41.420 --> 00:00:48.140
On your phone or laptop, there are three
tabs: Exercise, Notes and Messages.

11
00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:52.141
Exercise shows what the room sees, what to
watch for,

12
00:00:52.141 --> 00:00:56.900
and which departments have answered, but
never what they wrote.

13
00:00:59.450 --> 00:01:02.871
To log a note, open Notes and tap the
type:

14
00:01:02.871 --> 00:01:07.060
Positive, Needs improvement, or Critical
gap.

15
00:01:07.610 --> 00:01:12.510
Check the department; it is filled in when
the inject names one.

16
00:01:12.810 --> 00:01:16.890
Write a few sentences, and press Log note.

17
00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:23.850
Prefer to speak? Tap the microphone,
speak, and tap it again.

18
00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:30.130
Correct the words, then press Log note;
speaking alone never sends anything.

19
00:01:30.680 --> 00:01:34.810
Note what the team did, and what the plan
says.

20
00:01:35.110 --> 00:01:39.740
Where there is no plan, note what the
inject asked for.

21
00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:42.560
Never name a person.

22
00:01:43.110 --> 00:01:48.220
If something would stop the response
altogether, choose Critical gap.

23
00:01:48.520 --> 00:01:52.460
Your note reaches the facilitator straight
away.

24
00:01:55.010 --> 00:01:57.914
To reach the facilitator, open Messages,

25
00:01:57.914 --> 00:02:03.770
tap a ready-made line such as Our room
needs more time, and press Send.

26
00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:07.820
Or type your own message and press Send.

27
00:02:08.120 --> 00:02:11.940
It goes for your room, not under your
name.

28
00:02:12.490 --> 00:02:16.860
Replies stay at the top until you press
Got it or Reply.

29
00:02:19.410 --> 00:02:22.750
Took a call, or locked your screen?

30
00:02:23.050 --> 00:02:28.570
Nothing is lost. The page catches up by
itself.

31
00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:35.240
If your device restarts, open the same
link and press Continue on Welcome back.

32
00:02:35.540 --> 00:02:41.280
Logged notes are saved, and an unfinished
note comes back on the same device.

33
00:02:41.830 --> 00:02:46.970
If a participant loses their page, tap
Show join code.

34
00:02:47.270 --> 00:02:51.180
Your screen fills with the code for them
to scan.

35
00:02:51.730 --> 00:02:56.480
After the end, your notes stay open for up
to five hours.

36
00:02:56.780 --> 00:03:00.240
Then please answer the one-minute survey.

37
00:03:00.790 --> 00:03:07.370
To recap. Watch, never guide, and log
notes with Log note.

38
00:03:07.670 --> 00:03:11.770
Critical gap reaches the facilitator at
once.

39
00:03:12.070 --> 00:03:16.530
Show join code helps anyone who loses
their page.

40
00:03:17.080 --> 00:03:22.770
Please set your phone or laptop to silent
now. Thank you.

